1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,940
My dad, George, only had an eighth-grade education.
我的父亲乔治只受过八年级的教育。

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:09,600
A quiet man, he didn’t understand my world of school activities.
他是个沉默寡言的人，不懂我在学校里那些活动的世界。

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,590
From age 14, he worked.
他从十四岁起就开始工作了。

4
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:18,890
And his dad, Albert, took the money my dad earned and used it to pay family expenses.
他的父亲艾伯特把我爸挣的钱拿去，用来支付家里的开销。

5
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:30,620
I didn’t really understand his world either: He was a livestock trucker and I thought that I would surpass anything he had accomplished by the time I walked across the stage at high school graduation.
其实我也不太懂他的世界：他是个开卡车运牲口的司机，而我以为，等我走过高中毕业典礼的舞台时，我取得的成就会超过他所取得的一切。

6
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:41,360
Summers in the mid-70s were spent at home shooting baskets, hitting a baseball, or throwing a football, preparing for my future as a quarterback on a football team.
七十年代中期的那些夏天，我都待在家里投篮、击打棒球或扔橄榄球，为将来在橄榄球队当四分卫做准备。

7
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,760
In poor weather, I read about sports or practiced my trombone.
天气不好时，我就读读体育方面的书，或者练习吹长号。

8
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:52,820
The summer before my eighth grade I was one of a group of boys that a neighboring farmer hired to work in his field.
上八年级前的那个夏天，附近一位农场主雇了一群男孩到他的地里干活，我就是其中之一。

9
00:00:53,620 --> 00:01:00,990
He explained our basic task, the tractor fired up and we were off, riding down the field looking for weeds to spray with chemicals.
他给我们讲了讲基本的任务，拖拉机就发动起来，我们出发了，坐着车沿田地往下走，寻找要喷药的杂草。

10
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:06,210
After a short way, the farmer stopped and pointed at a weed which we had missed.
才走了一小段，农场主就停下来，指着一株我们漏掉的杂草。

11
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,290
Then we began again.
然后我们又重新开始。

12
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:19,320
This happened over and over, but we soon learned to identify different grasses like cockleburs, lamb’s-quarters, foxtails, and the king of weeds, the pretty purple thistle.
这样的事一再发生，不过我们很快就学会了辨认各种草，比如苍耳、藜、狗尾草，还有杂草之王——漂亮的紫色蓟。

13
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:25,780
It was tiring work, but I looked forward to the pay, even though I wasn’t sure how much it would amount to.
这活儿很累人，但我盼着拿工钱，尽管我也不确定会有多少。

14
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:30,580
At home, my dad said, “A job’s a big step to growing up.
回到家，爸爸说：“有份工作是长大成人的一大步。

15
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,850
I’m glad you will be contributing to the household.”
我很高兴你要为这个家出份力了。”

16
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:39,560
My dad’s words made me realize that my earnings might not be mine to do with as I wished.
爸爸的话让我意识到，我挣的钱也许不能由我随心所欲地支配。

17
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:45,895
My labors lasted about two weeks, and the farmer said there might be more work, but I wasn’t interested.
我干了大约两周，农场主说可能还会有活儿，可我没兴趣了。

18
00:01:46,695 --> 00:01:50,045
I decided it was not fair that I had to contribute my money.
我觉得非得把自己的钱交出来，这不公平。

19
00:01:50,845 --> 00:01:52,215
The pay arrived at last.
工钱终于到手了。

20
00:01:53,015 --> 00:01:56,045
I understood immediately what my parents were worried about.
我立刻明白了父母在担心什么。
